1
00:00:02,761 --> 00:00:09,561
== sync, corrected by elderman ==
@elder_man

2
00:00:09,749 --> 00:00:11,649
(Sheldon:)Who leaves their bike
in the hallway?

3
00:00:11,651 --> 00:00:12,981
(Sheldon:)You know,
if I knew how to ride one,

4
00:00:12,986 --> 00:00:14,216
(Sheldon:)I'd steal it.

5
00:00:15,088 --> 00:00:16,618
(Leonard:)Ignore him,

6
00:00:16,623 --> 00:00:19,153
(Leonard:)he's just cranky because Bert
from the geology lab

7
00:00:19,158 --> 00:00:20,158
(Leonard:)won a big grant.

8
00:00:20,159 --> 00:00:22,289
(Penny:)Oh, I heard him
interviewed on the radio!

9
00:00:22,295 --> 00:00:23,695
(Penny:)You know, when they
told him he won,

10
00:00:23,696 --> 00:00:25,726
(Penny:)he didn't believe it,
but then he did believe it.

11
00:00:25,732 --> 00:00:27,332
(Penny:)It was so funny.

12
00:00:28,701 --> 00:00:31,001
(Sheldon:)Who listens
to the radio anymore?

13
00:00:32,805 --> 00:00:34,735
(Amy:)Bert is studying the way
microbes in rocks

14
00:00:34,741 --> 00:00:37,041
(Amy:)can survive in extreme
environmental conditions.

15
00:00:37,043 --> 00:00:38,713
(Leonard:)They say it could be
a potential indicator

16
00:00:38,711 --> 00:00:40,011
(Leonard:)of life on other planets.

17
00:00:40,013 --> 00:00:41,213
(Penny:)You know what, I've met Bert.

18
00:00:41,214 --> 00:00:44,654
(Penny:)Isn't he an indicator
of life on other planets?

19
00:00:46,119 --> 00:00:48,289
(Sheldon:)You used to
make those jokes about me.

20
00:00:49,455 --> 00:00:51,725
(Sheldon:)Now everything is
Bert, Bert, Bert!

21
00:00:53,126 --> 00:00:54,326
(Amy:)You know, Sheldon,

22
00:00:54,327 --> 00:00:55,397
(Amy:)maybe if you take the time

23
00:00:55,395 --> 00:00:56,725
(Amy:)to actually
read Bert's research,

24
00:00:56,729 --> 00:00:58,299
(Amy:)you'd be less bitter
about him winning.

25
00:00:58,298 --> 00:01:00,028
(Sheldon:)You want me to read

26
00:01:00,033 --> 00:01:01,733
(Sheldon:)a geology paper?

